#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Live test of the island in the running shell: sends real notifications
# over D-Bus, asks the island what it shows through its test IPC
# (Probe.qml, target "omarchy-buddy.test") and checks Omarchy's
# "notifications" IPC, omarchy-notification-wait, Claude requests through
# the real hook (a Codex one too, long questions, a long plan, a cut command, a diff, a queue, a
# question while its terminal has the focus, also
# in English at the largest zoom: every button inside the window or
# reachable by scrolling, ProbeLogic.layout), a finished agent run (a pop-up,
# no news item, #173), a pop-up with many buttons,
# the history (unfolding, "alle löschen" and undo), the settings page with
# invalid values, the player window (tests/fake-player, Spotify's +
# through tests/fake-hyprctl), Omarchy 4.5's
# act, keyboard, invokeAction, count and omarchy-actions buttons, O-Morchy's
# emotions (#177: played by their events, the stronger one wins) and the shell's log.
#
#   tests/live              run once, you at the PC
#   tests/live --teilen     also the Ruhemodus while the screen is shared
#                           (asks you to start a screen share, e.g. in the browser)
#   tests/live --warten     first wait until you are back and the island is
#                           quiet (bin/omarchy-buddy-check after an update);
#                           leaves out "alle löschen" in the history
#
# Test notifications come from the app "Buddy-Test" and are taken out of
# the history again at the end; the Ruhemodus is put back as it was. Exit
# code 0: all good, 1: something failed, 2: the island does not answer,
# 3: it failed only while something real was on the island (disturbed();
# bin/omarchy-buddy-check then tries again later).

